<p>On the basis of exchange rates from 21-26 June, sterling's average RMG is greater than +5 per cent at 5.035. It is therefore currently forecast to enter the first of up to five confirmation periods on 1 July, prior to a possible revaluation on 20 August. The next largest RMG is that of the Italian lira at 2.599 per cent. The negative threshold is therefore -2 per cent (minimum possible). As there are no currenncies with average RMGs below this threshold, no green rate changes are currently forecast from 1 July.</p>
